<Solution>
  <!--
    THE MOBILE HEADS, IN A SOLUTION OF THEIR OWN.

    Not because they are a different kind of project - they are composition roots and every group A
    rule governs them - but because Broiler.VM.slnx must build on a machine with the .NET SDK and
    nothing else. These target frameworks need a workload, and the iOS one needs Xcode, so folding
    them into the main solution would make the build a contributor runs before pushing fail without
    an installation this component has never required.

    ComponentGraph.SolutionFiles names this file. A project listed in neither solution is one no
    rule governs, and rule A14 reports it rather than letting it be invisible.
  -->
  <Folder Name="/compositions/">
    <Project Path="src/compositions/Broiler.VM.Composition.JavaScript.Android/Broiler.VM.Composition.JavaScript.Android.csproj" />
  </Folder>
</Solution>
